From 6eb727fcda4b984dbffe4eb5b5dd6deb1ea89cce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luciano Radrigan <lucianoradrigan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:17:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Cont1QC: clamp the armature current at zero (discontinuous
 conduction)

ContOneQuadrantConverter returned the full supply voltage whenever the current was
negative, held for the whole step, which injected energy: an unloaded motor at duty 0
accelerated from 150 to 182 rad/s in 0.5 s with i down to -145 A.

- converter returns the duty cycle for every current sign and declares
  blocks_negative_current
- SCMLSystem clamps that current at zero in the ODE right-hand side and after each
  integration, for motors with a single current; warns where the clamp is not
  implemented (two currents, multi converter)
- docs note, changelog entry
- tests: duty-0 coasting, continuous conduction identical to Cont2QC, braking with
  friction only slows the motor, warning for a two-current motor; the existing
  _convert test now expects the duty cycle for negative current
