index db5d8d03..256730e3 100644
--- a/docs/parts_gem/physical_systems/converters/1QC.rst
+++ b/docs/parts_gem/physical_systems/converters/1QC.rst
@@ -13,6 +13,19 @@ Discrete One Quadrant Converter
 Continuous One Quadrant Converter
 '''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''
 
+.. note::
+   A one-quadrant converter cannot carry a negative output current. When the motor's induced voltage
+   exceeds the commanded average voltage, the current falls to zero and stays there (discontinuous
+   conduction) and the machine coasts. For DC motors with a single current (permanently excited,
+   series) the physical system clamps the current at zero during integration. For motors with two
+   currents (shunt, externally excited) and inside a multi converter the clamp is not applied, and a
+   warning is issued.
+
+   The clamp acts on the right-hand side of the ODE, so a solver that subdivides the step (the default
+   ``ScipyOdeSolver``) stops the current at its zero crossing inside the step. A fixed-step solver
+   such as ``EulerSolver`` clamps it at the end of its step. The model stays the averaged one: the
+   duty-cycle voltage is applied while the current is positive.
+
 .. autoclass:: gym_electric_motor.physical_systems.converters.ContOneQuadrantConverter
    :members:
    :inherited-members:
